---
const base = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/').replace(/\/+$/, '');
const installUrl = `${base}/docs/getting-started/installation/`;
const docsUrl = `${base}/docs/`;
const questions = [
  ['What is Koamishin Auth?', 'Koamishin Auth is an open-source, self-hosted centralized authentication and user identity platform for Laravel and modern web applications.'],
  ['How do I self-host Koamishin Auth?', 'You can get started in minutes using Docker Compose with Octane and PostgreSQL, or deploy manually on any PHP 8.4+ environment with SQLite, MySQL, or PostgreSQL.'],
  ['What features are included out of the box?', 'Independent application environments (development vs production), OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect with PKCE, scoped management APIs, Svix-compatible signed webhooks, Passkeys (WebAuthn), TOTP 2FA, social login (GitHub, Google, Facebook), and official Laravel and JavaScript SDKs.'],
  ['Can applications isolate user accounts?', 'Yes. Each application environment maintains its own isolated user directory (identity namespace). The same email or username can register in multiple applications without unique constraint collisions.'],
  ['Is there an OAuth consent screen for my own apps?', 'By default, first-party applications skip the OAuth consent prompt for seamless login and registration. You can toggle explicit consent on or off per application in the admin panel.'],
  ['What SDKs are available?', 'Official PHP / Laravel SDK (koamishin/auth-php) and browser JavaScript/TypeScript SDK (@koamishin/auth-js), with zero-config route handling, token refresh, and request guards.'],
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Koamishin Auth — Open-source, self-hosted centralized authentication and user identity platform for Laravel and modern web apps." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f5f4ee" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}/koamishin-logo.svg`} />
    <title>Koamishin Auth | Self-Hosted Centralized Authentication</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="header shell">
      <a class="brand" href={`${base}/`} aria-label="Koamishin Auth home"><img src={`${base}/koamishin-logo.svg`} alt="" width="36" height="36" /><span>koamishin<span class="brand-light"> / auth</span></span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#features">Features</a><a href="#questions">FAQ</a><a class="docs-link" href={docsUrl}>Documentation</a><a class="nav-link" href={installUrl}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> OPEN-SOURCE CENTRALIZED AUTH</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Own your<br />identity layer.</h1>
          <p class="hero-description">Koamishin Auth is the self-hosted authentication platform for developers. Connect multiple apps with isolated identities, OAuth 2.0 PKCE, passkeys, webhooks, and official Laravel and JS SDKs.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button" href={installUrl}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a class="button button-outline" href={docsUrl}>Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note">Self-hosted with Docker or PHP 8.4+ · MIT Licensed · Production-ready</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="art-top"><span>KOAMISHIN AUTH</span><span>IDENTITY / ACCESS</span></div>
          <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><div class="orbit orbit-three"></div>
          <div class="art-center"><img src={`${base}/koamishin-logo.svg`} alt="" width="72" height="72" /><span>CENTRAL AUTH</span></div>
          <span class="art-node node-one">01 <b>MULTI-TENANT</b></span><span class="art-node node-two">02 <b>OAUTH2 PKCE</b></span><span class="art-node node-three">03 <b>SDK CONNECTED</b></span>
          <div class="art-bottom"><span>SELF-HOSTED PLATFORM</span><span>● &nbsp; CONNECTED</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="features" class="intro shell">
        <div class="section-label"><span>01 / PLATFORM CAPABILITIES</span><span>EVERYTHING YOU NEED TO SHIP</span></div>
        <div class="intro-grid"><h2>Centralized auth.<br /><span>Isolated identities.</span></h2><p>Deploy one authentication server that powers all your applications. Users register through your apps, credentials stay isolated, and sessions synchronize seamlessly via modern SDKs.</p></div>
        <div class="features">
          <article><span class="feature-number">01</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">❖</div><h3>Isolated Environments</h3><p>Separate development and production user directories per application. Identical emails can exist in different apps without conflict.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">02</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚡</div><h3>Seamless First-Party Sign-In</h3><p>OAuth consent prompts are skipped by default for your own applications. Users log in or register and return straight to your app.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">03</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔐</div><h3>Modern Credentials</h3><p>Publishable and Secret keys (pk_..., sk_...), standard S256 PKCE, Passkeys (WebAuthn), and TOTP two-factor authentication.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">04</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">📦</div><h3>Official SDKs</h3><p>Drop-in Laravel SDK (koamishin/auth-php) with route guards, and zero-dependency browser JS/TS SDK (@koamishin/auth-js).</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">05</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔔</div><h3>Signed Webhooks</h3><p>Deliver user lifecycle events (user.created, user.updated) in real-time with standard Svix signature verification.</p></article>
          <article><span class="feature-number">06</span><div class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">📊</div><h3>Filament Admin Panel</h3><p>Manage organizations, applications, keys, roles, sessions, and view realtime activity logs through an intuitive dashboard.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="statement"><div class="shell statement-inner"><p class="eyebrow">READY IN MINUTES</p><h2>Deploy on your own infrastructure.<br /><span>Zero vendor lock-in.</span></h2><a href={installUrl}>Get started with self-hosting <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
      <section id="questions" class="faq shell"><div class="section-label"><span>02 / FREQUENTLY ASKED</span><span>QUESTIONS &amp; ANSWERS</span></div><div class="faq-grid"><div><h2>Everything you need<br />to know.</h2><p>Common questions about self-hosting, architecture, and integrating Koamishin Auth.</p></div><div class="faq-list">{questions.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></section>
      <section class="closing shell"><div><p class="eyebrow">TAKE CONTROL OF YOUR IDENTITY LAYER</p><h2>Start self-hosting<br />Koamishin Auth today.</h2></div><a class="button button-light" href={installUrl}>Get started now <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="footer shell"><a class="brand" href={`${base}/`}><img src={`${base}/koamishin-logo.svg`} alt="" width="32" height="32" /><span>koamishin<span class="brand-light"> / auth</span></span></a><p>Centralized authentication, thoughtfully crafted.</p><a href="#main">Back to top ↑</a></footer>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap');
